  "description": "SendGrid Email API emulator, runnable as a project and consumable from any Aspire AppHost. A single assembly that bundles the in-process emulator server (speaking the real SendGrid v3 Mail Send REST API — POST /v3/mail/send returning 202 + X-Message-Id) and the AppHost integration. Because the SendGrid SDK hard-codes https://api.sendgrid.com and reads no configuration of its own, the emulator intercepts the wired consumer's HTTPS egress with a per-app MITM proxy (HTTPS_PROXY + a trusted CA injected into only that process): consumers keep the real SendGrid client unchanged — no code change, not even the API key is required to change. Captured emails are viewable in a built-in Mailpit-style web dashboard and queryable over a REST API (both on-demand), and can be persisted as .eml to Blob storage.",
  "id": "Blaztrap.Aspire.Hosting.SendGrid",
